fecting scores better (0 vs 2, 4 vs 5), so the verdict doesn't hinge on priors. I'm going with submit.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm treating this as a twin prisoner's dilemma with different observations, so the other copy runs the same function on a different input. My intervention on this copy's node doesn't touch the other's, and since the inputs differ, the other's action looks like a separate node that stays at its prior and doesn't depend on mine. That makes defecting the dominant choice, so I'm leaning toward sending the letter. I'm still weighing whether the inputs could be treated as symmetric relabelings.\n\nI'm checking whether treating the inputs as symmetric relabelings changes anything, but the essay says different inputs mean different nodes. Even with the other node fixed at any prior, defecting scores better (0 vs 2, 4 vs 5), so the verdict doesn't hinge on priors. I'm going with submit.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":8042,"completion_tokens":580,"total_tokens":8622,"cost":0.043768,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.043768,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.032168,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.0116},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":273,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}